Z||000000||M King||12-30-1999||11:53 PM||||I have a few quick fiero questions. First of all I was wondering what kind of seat colors came in the fieros. I know that they only had leather in the 88's. But I have seen allot of pics with some fieros haveing two-tone cloth seats. If they ever came with the two-tone what years and what colors could you get? Also I was wondering if the four cylinder fieros were OHC or OHV. I haven't heard/seen of many OHV four bangers. So does this make a a kind of "rare" engine type? Or do I just have my OHV and OHC mixed up? THANKS ALLOT! Sorry about the long post but im kinda board. <p>[This message has been edited by M King (edited 12-30-1999).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||12-31-1999||12:36 AM||||Lets see if I can get this right. 84SE came with the striped ones. 85SE/GT came with two tone. Both 84and 85 base came with solid. all with speakers. 86 and up SE/GT came with the ones with the fake leather stripe and logo. Does this help.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||12-31-1999||12:37 AM||||Oh yes then there was the 84 pigskin and sheepskin seats. Only on red fully loaded cars.||||reg||1
