Z||000004||TOM||12-31-1999||01:31 AM||||Yeah kind on like cow skin. But I guess leather is ok.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||12-31-1999||02:43 AM||||My 88 doesn't have leather seats, they are grey cloth. My friend's 86 GT has a different style solid grey cloth, my 85 has two tone light/dark grey. Simply put, you have grey or tan with a few odd combinations that show up every once in a while.<BR>The 4 cyl is a GM 2.5 "Iron Duke" with a typical OHV/ cam in block/pushrod valvetrain. The 4 cyl cars are fun to drive, just not the most powerful.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-31-1999||04:14 AM||||I think you could get the sheepskin seats on certain '85s, too.  I know of 2 '85s with them and they aren't fully loaded or red, but they are 100% original.||||reg||1
Z||000007||dogtired||12-31-1999||04:46 AM||||M King<BR>Its ok for the long post cause your KINDA Board  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The rest of US are REAL board, that is why we are answering it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Does Mark Corbins "Fiero Spotters Guide" talk about seats? I have one, just to board to go look it up?<P>Really I thought there were only 2 seats!<BR>The Drivers and Passengers  NO  NO I mean<BR>Gray and Tan? or Leather and Lumbar?<P>OK MonkeyMan where did you hide my Drugs?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
