Z||000009||batboy||12-31-1999||09:50 AM||||Since nobody answered MKing's OHC question, I'm up to it. American auto makers have not gotten into the overhead cam engine thing as much as the Japanese companies have. There is one GM OHC 4 cylinder that immediately comes to mind, the Quad 4 which has 4 overhead cams in the head that run 16 valves (4 per cylinder). Some people have swapped this engine into Fieros. We have a couple old topics discussing this. I personally feel there are better engine conversion candidates for the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Rob||12-31-1999||07:48 PM||||  The fleece and suede seats came in the 84 and 85 Fieros only. It was an option that could be ordered in any model but it had to have the tan interior as the seats came in med. doeskin only.  ||||reg||1
